     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis. A single 1700 mg dose is also higher than any standard per-dose amount.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** at a different frequency\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is really what you intend, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose."
      }
